# component: slider
# decisions: A11Y-5, DOC-1, DOC-2, FOC-1, FOC-6, FRM-4
# hunks:
#   FOC-1, FOC-6: the thumb's `ring-ring/50` colour and its three glow triggers (`hover:ring-3`,
#     `focus-visible:ring-3`, `active:ring-3`) are removed, along with
#     `focus-visible:outline-hidden`, which would have suppressed the global outline on a control
#     that is not text entry.
#   FRM-4: `disabled:pointer-events-none` is dropped, so a disabled slider stays hoverable and a
#     Tooltip can explain it.
#   A11Y-5: the root's `aria-label` is forwarded to each thumb through `getAriaLabel`. Base UI keeps
#     the real control in a visually hidden `<input type="range">` inside the thumb, and an
#     `aria-label` on the root lands on a `<div>` with no role — so upstream's file ships a NAMELESS
#     `role="slider"` in every composition, including its own docs examples (axe: `label`,
#     critical). `getAriaLabel` is the only prop Base UI forwards to that input. FLAGGED FOR MK
#     rather than decided silently: A11Y-5 is the accessible-name row, but its letter is the
#     `", "` separator. A range slider gives both thumbs the group's name — upstream has no
#     per-thumb label API, and the fork's `thumbAriaLabels` is gone with the fork.
#   cn: `import { cn } from "cn"` becomes `@vegastack/design` — our npm layer owns `cn` (DOC-2).
#   formatting: the repository formatter (prettier defaults: semicolons, trailing commas)
#               reflows the file, and `registry-stamp.mjs` writes the provenance header the
#               three-copy model needs (DOC-1); those hunks carry no decision of their own.
